# Frontend (Next.js) Conventions

## Critical: Next.js 16

This is NOT standard Next.js. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing App Router code. Heed deprecation notices.

## Stack

- App Router in `src/app/`
- Data fetching: `@tanstack/react-query` hooks in `src/hooks/`
- HTTP client: `src/lib/api.ts` (axios + JWT interceptor)
- UI: shadcn/ui in `src/components/ui/`
- State: Zustand for client state; React Query for server state
- Forms: react-hook-form + Zod

## API calls

```typescript
import api from "@/lib/api";
const { data } = await api.get("/tickets");
```

Token is auto-attached from `localStorage`. 401 redirects to `/login`.

## Labels & enums

All Arabic labels for statuses, priorities, types, roles → `src/lib/constants.ts`.
Backend enum keys stay English; display labels are Arabic.

## Role-based UI

Hide actions the user's role cannot perform. Backend still enforces — UI hiding is UX only.

## Components

- Shared: `src/components/shared/` (EmptyState, LoadingSpinner, etc.)
- Layout: `src/components/layout/` (Sidebar, etc.)
- Pages: thin — delegate to hooks and shared components

## Loading

- Page and list data: matching skeleton from `LoadingSpinner.tsx` (`SkeletonList`, `SkeletonTable`, `SkeletonTicketDetail`, …)
- `FullPageLoading` is only the AppShell auth gate on first hydrate — not tab switches
- Do not show a spinner and then a skeleton on the same navigation

## Responsive

Every screen must work from ~360px up. Read `.cursor/rules/responsive-ui.mdc` before adding or restyling UI.

## Dropdowns

Never use native `<select>`. Pick the control by list length:

- **≤ ~8 options, all visible at once:** `BrmOptionList` inside `BrmPanel`
- **Compact picker (relation kind, difficulty, …):** `ThemeSelect`

Placeholders live in `SELECT_PLACEHOLDERS` (`constants.ts`). Enum labels stay in their own maps (`DIFFICULTY_LABELS`, `PRIORITY_LABELS`, …).

## Modals & picker panels

### Overlay dialogs (confirm, forms)

Every blocking dialog uses the same shell — do not invent a one-off layout.

- **Backdrop:** `fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-center justify-center p-4`, `background: rgba(0,0,0,0.6)`, `backdropFilter: blur(4px)`; click backdrop to dismiss when safe
- **Card:** `palette-modal brm-modal rounded-2xl overflow-hidden`, `max-w-md` or `max-w-lg`, `background: var(--card)`, `border: 1px solid var(--border)`, shadow `0 24px 64px rgba(0,0,0,0.3)`
- **Header:** icon tile (`w-9 h-9 rounded-xl`, brand or warning tint) + bold title; dismiss with X or `إلغاء`
- **Body:** last child scrolls — `.brm-modal` caps height at `min(90dvh, 100% - 2rem)`

References: `ConfirmModal` in `tickets/[id]/page.tsx`, `Modal` in `users/page.tsx`, revoke/reject flows in `invitations/page.tsx`.

### Inline picker panels (expand-in-place)

Short lists and add flows that open inside a card (relations, filters) use shared building blocks:

- **`BrmPanel`** — muted panel; full header (icon + title + cancel) when standalone, or `embedded` when the parent card already has the section title
- **`ThemeSelect`** — relation kind, difficulty, and other compact enum pickers
- **`BrmOptionList`** — only when every option should stay visible in the panel
- Search result rows inside a panel reuse **`brm-list-choice`** hover styling

Never use native `<select>` in these panels. Reference: `TicketDependencies.tsx`.

## Styling

- Tailwind CSS 4 with brand colors from `req.md` §17
- RTL-first: layout assumes `dir="rtl"` on `<html>`
